                'Clark–Fisher model: as countries develop, employment shifts from primary to secondary, then to tertiary and quaternary (e.g. UK about 1% primary, 16% secondary, over 80% tertiary; Ethiopia over 60% primary). Triangular graphs are used to show this.',
