                'If the trial balance does not agree, the difference is placed in a suspense account temporarily so that statements can be drafted; it is cleared when errors are found.',
                'Only errors that affected the trial balance go through the suspense account; the six non-affecting errors are corrected between the two ledger accounts concerned.',
                'After corrections, recalculate profit: corrections to income or expense accounts change profit; corrections to asset/liability accounts (e.g. bank, trade receivables) do not.',
