                'Capital expenditure buys or improves non-current assets that last more than a year, including costs of getting them ready for use: delivery, installation, legal fees, extensions. It appears in the statement of financial position.',
                'Revenue expenditure is day-to-day running cost or maintenance: wages, fuel, repairs, insurance, rent. It is charged to the income statement.',
