                'Comparability: users can compare a firm with previous years and with other firms — requires consistent policies.',
                'Relevance: information helps users make economic decisions and is available in time to be useful.',
                'Reliability: information is free from material error and bias and can be depended on (faithful representation).',
                'Understandability: information is presented clearly so users with reasonable business knowledge can understand it.',
                'Sometimes the objectives conflict, e.g. very reliable information may take too long to produce to be relevant; accountants must balance them.',
