                'Succession: Sunni Muslims accepted Abu Bakr, then Umar, Uthman and Ali as the four Rightly Guided Caliphs; Shiah Muslims believe Ali (cousin and son-in-law) was the Prophet’s chosen successor at Ghadir Khumm, followed by twelve Imams, the last (Imam al-Mahdi) in occultation.',
                'Hajj (8th–13th Dhul Hijjah): ihram (two white sheets, equality), tawaf (seven circuits of the Kabah), say between Safa and Marwa (Hajar’s search), Zamzam water, the stand at Arafat by the Mount of Mercy (the peak of Hajj, seeking forgiveness), night at Muzdalifah collecting pebbles, stoning the pillars at Mina (rejecting Satan), sacrifice and shaving the head.',
                'Umrah is the "lesser pilgrimage": can be done any time, is not compulsory, and includes ihram, tawaf and say but not Arafat, Muzdalifah or Mina.',
