              workedExample:`Q (c) "Hajj is too difficult to be worthwhile today." Evaluate. [8]
Difficulties: cost; over 1.8 million pilgrims (2024) in heat above 45°C; deaths from heat stroke and past crowd crushes (e.g. Mina 2015).
Worth it: fulfils a pillar; forgiveness of sins (hadith: returns "as the day his mother bore him"); experience of equality and unity of the ummah; Saudi improvements — Makkah Metro, cooling systems, visa quotas.
Islamic principle: Hajj is required only of those who are physically and financially able (Quran 3:97), so the difficulty is already allowed for.
Judgement: worthwhile — the spiritual rewards outweigh hardships, and Islam excuses those unable.`,
